   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 384 of the laws of 1998 amending the public\nauthorities law relating to the powers of Terence Cardinal Cooke health care\ncenter, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7480",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7480-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §5, Chap 384 of 1998",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7480\n\nSPONSOR: SERRANO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 384 of the laws of 1998 amending the public\nauthorities law relating to the powers of Terence Cardinal Cooke health\ncare center, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would extend for an additional five years the authority of\nthe-Terence Cardinal Cooke health care center to avail itself of Dormi-\ntory Authority construction management and financial services.  The\ncenter's current authority expires on December 31, 2023, and this would\nextend it until December 31, 2028.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would amend section 5 of chapter 384 of the laws of 1998 to\nchange the effective date so that NYSARC continues to have authority to\navail itself of Dormitory Authority construction and management finan-\ncial services for another five years.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTerence Cardinal Cooke Health Care Center has delivered exceptional\nlong- and short-term care and other vital health services to people with\ndiverse health and social needs since 1978. Located in the upper end of\nNew York's Central Park, it is home to: nurses skilled in 24-hour care\nin a traditional nursing home setting, premiere sub-acute rehabilitation\nprogram that eases the transition from hospital to home for people\nrecovering from a major illness or surgery, as well as a specialty\nhospital.for children and young adults with profound developmental disa-\nbilities and other extraordinary medical needs. This legislation will\nallow the organization to be eligible for financing and construction\nservices through the Dormitory Authority of the State of New York.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA.10813/58822 of 2018, SIGNED CHAP. 174\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
